.TH INSTALL-CONTROLROOM.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom-setup 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
install\-controlroom.sh \- install the control\-room bin area on a DAQ host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash install\-controlroom.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs on a DAQ host as the session account, from an unpacked payload
directory; normally invoked by
.BR "crs\-remote install" .
It:
.IP 1. 4
creates
.IR $CRS_HOME/bin ,
.IR $CRS_HOME/etc ,
.I $CRS_HOME/log
and
.IR ~/.crs ;
.IP 2. 4
installs
.BR start\-vnc\-session.sh ,
.BR stop\-vnc\-session.sh ,
.BR status\-vnc\-session.sh ,
.BR vnc\-discovery\-responder.py ,
.B crs\-app
and
.B crs\-provision\-desktop
into
.I bin
(mode 0755);
.IP 3. 4
installs
.I controlroom.yaml
and
.I apps.yaml
(0644) and
.I xstartup
(0755) into
.IR etc ;
.IP 4. 4
appends, once, a marker\-guarded PATH stanza to
.IR ~/.bash_profile ;
.IP 5. 4
for every inventory entry whose
.IR install_path / start
or
.IR install_path / stop
exists, replaces
.IB $CRS_HOME /bin/ script
with a symbolic link to it.
.PP
Step 5 needs
.BR python3 .
It does not install
.B mu2edaq\-discovery
for that interpreter; the responder sidecar then falls back to its
embedded copy of the protocol, and
.B mu2edaq\-discover
is not provided for the GUI's gateway scan.
The links of step 5 are what
.BR crs\-app (1)
executes; see the warning there.
.PP
Idempotent.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.IR ~/controlroom/{bin,etc,log} ,
.IR ~/.bash_profile .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_HOME
install area (default
.IR ~/controlroom ).
Note that
.BR crs\-remote (1)
and the PATH stanza assume the default.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; the failing command's status otherwise
.RB ( "set \-e" ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
crs\-remote install \-\-session shift\-main     # normal use
cd ~/.crs\-payload && bash install\-controlroom.sh   # by hand
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-remote (1),
.BR crs\-app (1),
.BR start\-vnc\-session.sh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group.
